  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 330 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe 08Z/3 am surface analysis shows expansive 1034 mb high \npressure over the upper Ohio river valley (northeast WV) and \nridging sw across the Ohio river valley and into the mid MS \nriver valley. Large high pressure continued clear skies across\nIL early this morning, with light SSE to calm winds. Seasonably\ncool temps ranged from 35-45F with mid 30s from Paris to\nRobinson, while NWS on east side of Lincoln was down to 34F. A\nfrontal boundary was over nw WI into southern MN, central \nNebraska to 1011 mb low pressure along the southern CO/KS \nborder.\n\nAnother high pressure system builds over the Great Lakes region\nby days end, while frontal boundary stays well north/nw of \nIL, while mid/upper level ridge into IL keeping us dry and the\nfront well to the north. Patchy frost possible east of I-55 \nuntil around 8 am, then a delightful fall day ahead with some \ncirrus clouds to spread eastward over central IL during this \nafternoon/evening. Though still ample sunshine today with light \nsouth winds. Highs today around 70F to lower 70s and dry \ndewpoints in the mid 30s to lower 40s. Good radiational cooling \nwill be in place again tonight with fair skies, light winds and \nlow dewpoints. Lows mostly in the lower 40s overnight with some \nupper 30s near the Indiana border. High pressure drifting over \nQuebec by sunset Tue while ridging sw across the Great Lakes and\ninto IL will provide a fair amount of sunshine Tue with light \neast/se winds and a bit milder highs 70-75F. Lows Tue night in \nthe low to mid 40s. Large high pressure over southeast Canada \nand New England Wed is ridging back into IL yet and provides \nsunshine with light to calm winds and highs in the low to mid \n70s. Ample sunshine and light winds again Thu with nearby high \npressure ridge and highs in the 70s.\n\nA blocking upper level pattern over the US this week with upper\nlevel lows/storm systems off the East Coast and the CA coast \nwith upper level ridging in nations mid section including IL. \nThe upper level ridge builds over IL late this week with a bit \nwarmer temps in mid to upper 70s Thu thru Sunday. Areas from \nSpringfield sw have a 20-30% chance of reaching near 80F this \nweekend. A stronger storm system moves across southern Canada \nthis weekend but consensus of models keeps qpf north and west of\nIL through early next week as above normal temperatures continue.\n\nThe Climate Prediction Center 6-10 Day Outlook for Oct 24-28 has\n65-75% chance of above normal temperatures over IL, while 40-50%\nchance of below normal precipitation in central IL and 50-55%\nchance below normal precipitation in southeast IL. So this\nweather pattern next two weeks looks good for the fall harvest \nof corn and soybeans in IL which is running ahead of schedule. \nCPC 8-14 Day Outlook for Oct 26-Nov 1 continues 65-75% chance of\nabove normal temperatures over IL while precipitation trending \nnear normal in eastern IL and slightly above normal (~35%) over \nwestern half of IL.",
